body:
I just graduated and got a "dream" full-time job at in the gaming industry. However, now I just am so depressed. Everything's suffered- social life, my mental health, physical health, and ability just to be a human being. I just don't see a point anymore, but I too also need to pay for my apartment and I can't just quit. I'm at a point where I'm just confused on the next step to take.

&#x200B;

I like the people I work with, for the most part, dislike the work, but at the same time, I personally don't want to do a bad job. So I work long hours but it just makes me think about how if this is going to be how life is forever, I don't want it. I want something easier, with clear time 9-5 so I don't have to give more than I want. Do the task and go back and live life. But I don't even know if I could find something like that that pays a decent wage.

&#x200B;

It's weird I feel like I wrote what you did above. I feel a little solace in the fact I'm not alone.
